  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to safe abortion in Mozambique - Access to Safe abortion in Mozambique 2017-2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Tillg&#xE5;ng till s&#xE4;ker abort i Mocambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ipas, a global organization based in the United States, has presented a project proposal aimed at contributing to the roll-out of safe abortion care in Mozambique. The three-year project to be implemented from 15 December 2016 to 31 December 2019 has a total budget of USD 10,000,000, of which SEK 47,060,000 (USD 5,060,000, USD 1 = SEK 9.30) is applied for from Sweden. Furthermore, parts of the total budget will also be financed by &quot;a large anonymous donor&quot; based in the USA and from Ipa&apos;s core support from the Netherlands.

The expected results of the project are:
1. To have contributed to the creation of a favorable and sustainable policy environment that promotes women&apos;s and girls&apos; access to safe abortion;
2. To have contributed to improved access and availability of safe abortion care and contraception for women and girls at more health care units;
Increased knowledge and action in young women and girls and strengthened social support networks;
4. New knowledge that is spread.

This will be achieved through advocacy work in various forums, technical support, dialogue with target groups and local communities, training of health staff and upgrading of care facilities.

The project, which has been designed in dialogue with the Ministry of Health and its partners, aims to help lay the foundation for the Ministry of Health to be able to plan for and offer nationwide abortion care and contraception in accordance with WHO guidelines. 

Ipas will implement the effort in collaboration with the Ministry of Health and other local partners such as the WHO, UNFPA, local and international civil society organizations, such as Pathfinder International and Population Services International (PSI), and research organizations.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ipas, som &#xE4;r en global organisation med s&#xE4;te i USA, har presenterat ett projekt f&#xF6;rslag &quot;Expansion av kvinnors och flickors tillg&#xE5;ng till s&#xE4;ker abort v&#xE5;rd och preventivmedel i Nampula och Zamb&#xE9;zia provinserna i Mo&#xE7;ambique&#x201D; som syftar till att bidra till utrullningen av s&#xE4;ker abortv&#xE5;rd i Mo&#xE7;ambique. Det tre-&#xE5;riga projektet ska genomf&#xF6;ras fr&#xE5;n 15 december 2016 till 31 december 2019 har en total budget p&#xE5; USD 10 000 000 varav SEK 47 060 000 (USD 5 060 000, USD 1=SEK 9,30) s&#xF6;ks fr&#xE5;n Sverige. Vidare kommer delar av den totala budgeten ocks&#xE5; att finansieras av &#x201D;en stor anonym givare&#x201D; baserad i USA och fr&#xE5;n Ipas k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d fr&#xE5;n Nederl&#xE4;nderna.

Den befintliga sjukv&#xE5;rdsinfrastrukturen i Mo&#xE7;ambique har dock begr&#xE4;nsad f&#xF6;rm&#xE5;ga att tillhandah&#xE5;lla s&#xE4;ker abort och preventivmedel till alla som beh&#xF6;ver, bl.a. p&#xE5; grund av brist p&#xE5; utbildad h&#xE4;lsopersonal, diskriminerande attityder, hinder f&#xF6;r regelbundna leveranser av sjukv&#xE5;rdsprodukter f&#xF6;r abort och preventivmedel. Kvinnor och flickor &#xE4;r ocks&#xE5; ofta omedvetna om sina r&#xE4;ttigheter och var man kan f&#xE5; tillg&#xE5;ng till dessa h&#xE4;lsotj&#xE4;nster.

Projektets f&#xF6;rv&#xE4;ntade resultat &#xE4;r:
1. Att ha bidragit till skapandet av en gynnsam och h&#xE5;llbar policymilj&#xF6; som fr&#xE4;mjar kvinnors och flickors tillf&#xE5;ng till s&#xE4;ker abort;
2. Att ha bidragit till f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrad tillg&#xE5;ng och tillg&#xE4;ngligheten till s&#xE4;ker abortv&#xE5;rd och preventivmedel f&#xF6;r kvinnor och flickor vid fler h&#xE4;lsov&#xE5;rdsenheter;
3. &#xD6;kad kunskap och handlingskraft hos unga kvinnor och flickor och st&#xE4;rkta sociala st&#xF6;dn&#xE4;tverk;
4. Ny kunskap som sprids.

Detta ska uppn&#xE5;s genom p&#xE5;verkansarbete inom olika forum, tekniskt st&#xF6;d, dialog med m&#xE5;lgrupper och lokalsamh&#xE4;llen, utbildning av h&#xE4;lsopersonal och uppgradering av v&#xE5;rdinr&#xE4;ttningar.

Ipas kommer att genomf&#xF6;ra insatsen i samarbete med h&#xE4;lsoministeriet och andra lokala partners s&#xE5;som WHO, UNFPA, lokala och internationella civilsamh&#xE4;llesorganisationer, s&#xE5;som Pathfinder International och Population Services International (PSI), och forskningsorganisationer.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the project is to improve the knowledge, ability, opportunities, and choices of women and girls in Mozambique to access safe, high-quality abortion care and contraception. Ipas would achieve this goal through the following four outcome areas:
&#x2022;outcome 1: support the creation of an enabling and sustained policy environment for access to safe abortion for women and girls.
&#x2022;outcome 2: improved availability and accessibility of services for girls and young women through multiple points of care. 
&#x2022;outcome 3: increased young womens and girls knowledge, agency and strengthened their social support networks; and
&#x2022;outcome 4: new knowledge generated and disseminated.</narrative>
  </description>
